\DOC simps

\TYPE {simps : unit -> thm list}

\SYNOPSIS
The theorems that have been declared into the simp set.

\DESCRIBE
A call {simps ()} returns the declared theorems, in the order in which
they were declared.

The simp set is global. Inside the load of a development that is
deterministic, because the files load in one order; in a session where
something extra has been loaded by hand, a proof sees that too. {simps ()}
is there so that a proof can say what it saw.

\FAILURE
Never fails.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # simps ();;
  val it : thm list = []

  # add_simps (CONJUNCTS count);;
  # length (simps ());;
  val it : int = 4
}

\SEEALSO
add_simp, add_simps, del_simp, simp_ss.

\ENDDOC
